// A C function with the system calling convention, and the symbol it lowers to.
//
// 'extern' says GetTickCount is defined elsewhere; '@c(system)' says its name is
// a C name and its calling convention the platform's system one. An 'extern'
// system function is also imported from a DLL, which is what the IR line
// records.
//
// It compiles rather than runs because the one system routine every Windows
// build has, GetTickCount from kernel32, is not something the runner links
// against; the declaration is the whole subject, and the call is there only so
// the optimizer has a reason to keep it.

extern fn @c(system) GetTickCount() u32;

fn ticks() u32 {
  GetTickCount();
}
